{"kind":"message","provenance":{"block_index":45,"record_type":"cursor.assistant_message"},"role":"assistant","text":"# Native Source-Session Audit\n\nRead-only inspection of all six corpus files. No files were edited.\n\n---\n\n## 1. `CORPUS_NOTE.txt` (83 bytes)\n\n| Aspect | Result |\n|--------|--------|\n| **Cursor Read tool** | **Fully decoded** — plain text returned verbatim |\n| **Shell/metadata only** | Not needed |\n\n**Decoded content:**\n- Line 1: `CURSOR_NATIVE_TEXT_MARKER COPPER_4821`\n- Line 2: blank\n- Line 3: `The portable document marker is ORBIT_2048.`\n\n**Markers:** `CURSOR_NATIVE_TEXT_MARKER`, `COPPER_4821`, `ORBIT_2048` (referenced, not defined here)\n\n---\n\n## 2. `timeline.py` (19 lines)\n\n| Aspect | Result |\n|--------|--------|\n| **Cursor Read tool** | **Fully decoded** — complete Python source |\n| **Shell/metadata only** | Not needed |\n\n**Decoded content:** A frozen `@dataclass Event` with `state`, `start_ms`, `end_ms`, plus `coalesce(events, gap_ms=0)` that merges consecutive same-state events when the inter-event gap is strictly less than `gap_ms`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. `corpus-card.png` (27,639 bytes)\n\n| Aspect | Result |\n|--------|--------|\n| **Cursor Read tool** | **Decoded image content** — visual representation returned (not raw bytes) |\n| **Shell (`file`, `identify`)** | Metadata only: PNG, **640×400**, 16-bit RGBA, non-interlaced |\n\n**Decoded visual facts (from Read image decode):**\n- **Shape:** Centered equilateral triangle on dark navy/charcoal background\n- **Colors:** Light/sky-blue triangle fill; pale lime-green border; white uppercase label; lime-green digits\n- **Text:** `BLUE TRIANGLE`\n- **Digits:** `7319`\n\n**Not established by Read alone:** Exact pixel dimensions (confirmed via shell: 640×400).\n\n---\n\n## 4. `corpus-document.pdf` (20,266 bytes)\n\n| Aspect | Result |\n|--------|--------|\n| **Cursor Read tool** | **Decoded document text** — PDF body text extracted |\n| **Shell (`file`, `pdftotext`)** | Confirmed PDF v1.4, 1 page; text matches Read output |\n\n**Decoded markers/content:**\n```\nNative session corpus\nDocument marker: ORBIT_2048\nThis disposable document tests whether a coding\nharness stores document attachments in its native\nsession history.\n```\n\n**Marker:** `ORBIT_2048` (matches `CORPUS_NOTE.txt` cross-reference)\n\n---\n\n## 5. `corpus-tone.wav` (8,078 bytes)\n\n| Aspect | Result |\n|--------|--------|\n| **Cursor Read tool** | **Failed** — `Binary files of type .wav are not supported` |\n| **Shell (`file`)** | Metadata only: RIFF WAVE, Microsoft PCM, 16-bit, mono, 16000 Hz |\n| **Shell (Python `wave` + FFT)** | **PCM fully decoded** |\n\n**Established audio facts (shell decode only):**\n| Property | Value |\n|----------|-------|\n| Channels | 1 (mono) |\n| Sample width | 16-bit |\n| Sample rate | 16,000 Hz |\n| Duration | 0.25 s (4,000 frames) |\n| Peak amplitude | ±4095 |\n| Dominant frequency | **440.0 Hz** (numpy FFT peak) |\n| Waveform | Sinusoidal tone, steady RMS ≈ 2895.8 |\n| Embedded text marker | **None** (only `Lavf58.76.100` encoder tag in INFO chunk) |\n\n---\n\n## 6. `corpus-transition.mp4` (2,540 bytes)\n\n| Aspect | Result |\n|--------|--------|\n| **Cursor Read tool** | **Failed** — `Cannot read binary files of type mp4` |\n| **Shell (`ffprobe`)** | Container/codec metadata decoded |\n| **Shell (`ffmpeg` frame extract)** | **Video pixels decoded** |\n\n**Established video facts (shell decode only):**\n| Property | Value |\n|----------|-------|\n| Codec | H.264 (avc1), High profile |\n| Resolution | **640×400** (matches PNG) |\n| Frame rate | 24 fps |\n| Duration | ~1.083 s (26 frames) |\n| Encoder | Lavf58.76.100 |\n| Audio stream | None |\n\n**Decoded pixel/color transition:**\n| Frames | Time (s) | Center RGB | Interpretation |\n|--------|----------|------------|----------------|\n| 0–12 | 0.000–0.500 | `(78, 155, 254)` | Solid light blue (matches PNG triangle fill) |\n| 13–25 | 0.542–1.042 | `(161, 228, 51)` | Solid lime green (matches PNG border/digits) |\n\nHard cut at **frame 13** (~0.542 s); no embedded text marker in container strings.\n\n---\n\n## 7. `timeline.py` Boundary Bug Analysis\n\nThe merge condition on line 14:\n\n```14:14:/tmp/sm-cursor-capture/xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx/work/timeline.py\n        if merged and merged[-1].state == event.state and event.start_ms - merged[-1].end_ms < gap_ms:\n```\n\n**Bug:** Strict `<` makes the tolerated gap interval **`[0, gap_ms)`** — exclusive at `gap_ms`.\n\n**Demonstrated behavior:**\n\n| Scenario | `gap_ms` | Gap (ms) | Merges? |\n|----------|----------|----------|---------|\n| Touching same-state (`end=100`, `start=100`) | 0 | 0 | **No** (`0 < 0` is false) |\n| Touching same-state | 1 | 0 | Yes (`0 < 1`) |\n| 1 ms separation (`end=100`, `start=101`) | 1 | 1 | **No** (`1 < 1` is false) |\n\n**Impact:**\n- With the default `gap_ms=0`, **adjacent/touching events with the same state never coalesce**, even when one ends exactly where the next begins. That is almost certainly unintended for a function named `coalesce` with a zero default.\n- For any `gap_ms > 0`, events separated by **exactly** `gap_ms` are excluded — an off-by-one at the inclusive boundary.\n\n**Fix (conceptual):** Use `<= gap_ms` if the contract is “merge when the gap is at most `gap_ms`”, or document that `gap_ms` is an exclusive upper bound (unusual for this API).\n\n---\n\n## Decode Summary\n\n| File | Read tool | Shell tools |\n|------|-----------|-------------|\n| `CORPUS_NOTE.txt` | Full text decode | — |\n| `timeline.py` | Full source decode | — |\n| `corpus-card.png` | Image/visual decode | Metadata (dimensions) |\n| `corpus-document.pdf` | Text decode | Metadata confirmation |\n| `corpus-tone.wav` | **Blocked** | Full PCM + 440 Hz tone |\n| `corpus-transition.mp4` | **Blocked** | Full container + frame pixels |\n\n**Cross-corpus markers verified:** `COPPER_4821` (text), `ORBIT_2048` (text + PDF), `7319` (image digits). Audio/video carry no alphanumeric markers—only measurable signal properties (440 Hz, blue→green color transition at frame 13).\n\nCURSOR_NATIVE_SOURCE_COMPLETE","timestamp_category":"absent"}
