{"kind":"message","provenance":{"block_index":4,"record_type":"cursor.assistant_message"},"role":"assistant","text":"## Prior markers (from memory)\n\n- **Text marker:** `COPPER_4821` (from `CURSOR_NATIVE_TEXT_MARKER COPPER_4821` in `CORPUS_NOTE.txt`)\n- **Image digits:** `7319` (on `corpus-card.png`)\n\n## `timeline.py` re-read (Read tool)\n\nLine 14 still uses strict less-than:\n\n```14:14:/tmp/sm-cursor-capture/xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx/work/timeline.py\n        if merged and merged[-1].state == event.state and event.start_ms - merged[-1].end_ms < gap_ms:\n```\n\n## Exact one-character boundary fix (not applied)\n\nChange the `<` before `gap_ms` to `<=`:\n\n```python\nevent.start_ms - merged[-1].end_ms <= gap_ms\n```\n\nThat single character makes gaps up to and including `gap_ms` mergeable, so touching same-state events coalesce when `gap_ms=0`.\n\nCURSOR_NATIVE_FOLLOWUP_COMPLETE","timestamp_category":"absent"}
